 "content": [
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "1. Description"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Two things, both in the Inventory Value spreadsheet download."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "One \u2014 the money comes through as text, not numbers.",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " Every money column is written the way the screen shows it, with a dollar sign and comma separators. Spreadsheet software reads that as words rather than numbers."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Two \u2014 the file ignores which columns you chose, and puts them in a different order from the screen.",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " If you switch "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Margin",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " or "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Total Sell",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " off on screen, they still appear in the file. And the columns come out in a different order: "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Total Cost",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " is ninth in the file but last on screen."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the money:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " the person downloading this is almost always downloading it in order to do sums \u2014 total the shelf, sort by value, chart it, paste it into a stock valuation. Because the money columns arrive as text, "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "none of that works",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " until they clean every column by hand first. A total comes out as zero, or as an error, and it is not obvious why."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the columns:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " someone who tidies the report down to the four columns they care about, then downloads it, gets all twelve back anyway. Their choice was silently ignored \u2014 no message, no explanation. And because the order differs from the screen, anyone who has built a template or a habit around the screen's layout finds the file does not match it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "rule"
  },
