          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " menu and choose "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Download (CSV)",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Open the file in Excel, Numbers or Google Sheets."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "The two columns you switched off are still there",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " \u2014 the file has all twelve."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Look at the order: "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Total Cost",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " sits ninth, not last, and "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Margin %",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " is the final column. On screen, Total Cost is last."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Now select any money column and try to total it. "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "You get nothing usable",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": ", because the cells are text. You can confirm it directly: the cell reads "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "$11,176.88",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "code"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " including the dollar sign and comma, which is why the spreadsheet treats it as words."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "For comparison, take the "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Download (PDF)",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " of the same view \u2014 that one is formatted correctly and is not part of this ticket."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "rule"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "4. Expected behaviour"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Both are written requirements in the Inventory Value specification, version 3."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the money",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " \u2014 the Story 10 context note, verbatim:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "blockquote",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "\"in the CSV, money values are written as "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "plain numbers with two decimals and no thousands separators",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " (so they "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "parse cleanly in a spreadsheet",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "); the PDF uses the same on-screen currency formatting with the '$' and thousands separators.\""
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Note that the requirement anticipated this exact problem \u2014 \"so they parse cleanly in a spreadsheet\" is the reason it is written that way. "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The PDF half is correct.",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " Only the spreadsheet breaches it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the columns",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " \u2014 requirement S10-R3, verbatim:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "blockquote",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "\"Both downloads include "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "only the columns currently shown",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", in the "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "same left-to-right order as the screen",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", with "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Total Cost last",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ".\""
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "That is three separate promises in one sentence, and the file breaks all three."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "rule"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "5. Current behaviour"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the money:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " every money column in the spreadsheet arrives as text \u2014 written exactly as the screen shows it, with a dollar sign and comma separators \u2014 so spreadsheet software reads it as words. Totals come out as zero or as an error, and it is not obvious why. The person has to clean every money column by hand before they can do any arithmetic."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On the columns:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " the file ignores which columns you chose. Switch "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Margin",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " or "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Total Sell",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " off on screen and they still appear in the file. The order is different too: "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Total Cost",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " is ninth in the file but last on screen."
    }
   ]
  },
